From cf23759d1df47a7a3e6c8eaf97fe90642c93d753 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Guohan Lu <securely1g@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 09:02:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Import reviewed APT locks without repeating package
 declarations

Add apt.import_lock to consume exact package URLs, SHA256 digests and dependency graphs from a version-2 lock. Image consumers can keep one reviewed lock instead of another generated MODULE list of every package version.

Reuse deb_import, deb_postfix and the dependency-set generator for independent data/control archives and complete package closures. Keep C++ discovery on apt.install, whose Contents indexes are absent from runtime locks. Validate package identity, architecture, hashes and graph completeness before creating repositories.

Origin: SONiC-maintained extension for sonic-buildimage PRs #30 and #13. Upstream apt/extensions.bzl at blob c82b0edb1fa57184c78d4d0ac8967aed00e7cbdf has no lock-import tag. This patch is maintained in securely1g/sonic-build-infra and applied after the existing rules_distroless 0.9.4.sonic.10 patch set.

Add regressions for transitive closures, cycles, architecture-independent packages, set selection and malformed lock inputs.

Signed-off-by: Guohan Lu <securely1g@gmail.com>
