 _doc = """
 Module extension to create Debian repositories.
 
+For a reviewed version-2 runtime lock, use `apt.import_lock` instead of repeating
+its package versions in `apt.install` declarations. This reads exact archive
+URLs and SHA256 digests from the lock and does not resolve package indexes or
+rewrite the lock:
+
+```starlark
+apt = use_extension("@rules_distroless//apt:extensions.bzl", "apt")
+apt.import_lock(lock = "//image:apt.lock.json")
+use_repo(apt, "image_packages")  # dependency-set name recorded in the lock
+```
+
+Every root and transitive package has independent `:data` and `:control` targets
+(e.g. `@image_packages//libc6:data`), plus its normal package-closure target.
+`dependency_sets = ["image_packages"]` can limit imports from a shared lock.
+The existing importer and deb_postfix rule still prepare the archives.
+Native C++ header/library exports continue to use `apt.install`: the runtime
+lock does not contain the Debian Contents-index data needed for those exports.
+
 Create Debian repositories with packages "installed" in them and available
 to use in Bazel.
 
